  tool='write' path='/02_distill/cards/2026-03-23__hn-vibe-coding-spam.md' content='# AI raises the baseline for convincing spam; visual heuristics break down\n\nSource: [HN: They\'re vibe-coding spam now](https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=47482760) → [Tedium](https://tedium.co/2026/02/25/vibe-coded-email-spam/)\n\n## The shift\n\nAI tools lower the friction barrier for producing *visually clean* spam and phishing emails. Attackers no longer need design skills to create messages that look professional and legitimate.\n\n## The risk\n\n- **Heuristic collapse**: People trained themselves to spot "obviously fake" design. That signal is gone.\n- **Skill floor drops**: Scam operations scale because they no longer need graphic designers.\n- **Trust smell emerges**: Ironically, generic AI design patterns *may* become a marker of suspicion over time, if they\'re identifiable.\n\n## The deeper problems\n\nHN commentary adds nuance:\n- Weak incentives in free email (Gmail doesn\'t charge, so filtering is secondary).\n- Attackers don\'t need *generation*—they copy real branded emails. Distribution and filtering matter as much as generation quality.\n- The problem is not AI alone; it\'s the *gap* between message quality and filtering infrastructure.\n\n## Implication\n\nVision-based defenses ("this looks fake") lose power; need better infrastructure-level signals (authentication, reputation, distribution patterns).\n' start_line=0 end_line=0
